    "id": "hld",
    "file": "hld.html",
    "title": "HLD: Scaling, Data & Distributed Systems",
    "groups": [
      {
        "group": "Distributed systems fundamentals",
        "slug": "distributed-systems-fundamentals",
        "mount": "#t-fundamentals",
        "items": [
          "Why go distributed: scale, availability, latency (and the network cost)",
          "CAP is per-operation: CP vs AP during a partition; PACELC's else-clause",
          "Consistency spectrum: strong / read-your-writes / eventual",
          "The latency ladder (memory ~100x SSD, cross-region ~300x same-DC)",
          "Availability math: nines as downtime; series multiplies, parallel adds nines"
        ]
      },
      {
        "group": "Load balancing",
        "slug": "load-balancing",
        "mount": "#t-load-balancing",
        "items": [
          "L4 vs L7 and what L7 buys (path routing, TLS, retries, rate limits)",
          "Algorithms: round robin, least connections, hash-on-key, weighted",
          "Active + passive health checks; connection draining",
          "Backends must be stateless; externalize session state",
          "Estimate fleet size from per-server QPS + peak factor + N+2 headroom"
        ]
      },
      {
        "group": "Consistent hashing",
        "slug": "consistent-hashing",
        "mount": "#t-consistent-hashing",
        "items": [
          "Why hash % N breaks: ~(N-1)/N of keys remap on resize",
          "The ring: key owned by first node clockwise; only ~K/N keys move",
          "Virtual nodes even out load and spread a failed node's share",
          "It balances key count, not traffic - hot keys still need help",
          "Placement not replication: store on next R distinct nodes for replicas"
        ]
      },
      {
        "group": "Caching",
        "slug": "caching",
        "mount": "#t-caching",
        "items": [
          "Cache-aside vs write-through vs write-back (and their failure modes)",
          "Eviction: LRU default, LFU, FIFO, TTL as a correctness knob",
          "Hit ratio drives backend load: 90%->95% halves DB QPS",
          "Size the cache from the hot-key fraction, not the full dataset",
          "Stampede protection: single-flight, locks, probabilistic early expiry"
        ]
      },
      {
        "group": "Transactions: ACID & isolation",
        "slug": "transactions-acid-isolation",
        "mount": "#t-transactions",
        "items": [
          "ACID: atomicity, consistency, isolation, durability (C is app-level)",
          "Anomalies: dirty read, non-repeatable read, phantom, lost update",
          "Isolation levels and what each permits (RC default allows lost update)",
          "Walk the lost-update race and its fixes (FOR UPDATE, atomic UPDATE, SI+retry)",
          "Write skew needs Serializable or a predicate lock; per-row locks don't help",
          "Hot-row write cap ~ 1000 / lock_hold_ms; shard the counter"
        ]
      },
      {
        "group": "SQL vs NoSQL decision framework",
        "slug": "sql-vs-nosql-decision-framework",
        "mount": "#t-sql-nosql",
        "items": [
          "Access pattern: narrow & known vs ad-hoc joins/aggregations",
          "Multi-record ACID need; write volume vs one primary node",
          "Schema stability; data shape (relational / document / graph / time-series)",
          "Consistency requirement: strong-by-default vs tunable quorums",
          "Default to Postgres; go polyglot per outgrown access pattern",
          "Compute the threshold before claiming 'we need NoSQL for scale'"
        ]
      },
      {
        "group": "Microservices trade-offs",
        "slug": "microservices-trade-offs",
        "mount": "#t-microservices",
        "items": [
          "Gains: independent deploy/scale, fault isolation, clear ownership",
          "Costs: distributed system, no cheap cross-service txns, ops surface",
          "It solves team-coordination scale, not traffic scale",
          "Fan-out math: 0.999^6 = 99.4%; parallelize + degrade non-critical calls",
          "Anti-patterns: distributed monolith, shared DB, nano-services, sync chains",
          "Start with a modular monolith; split by business capability"
        ]
      },
      {
        "group": "Distributed queues",
        "slug": "distributed-queues",
        "mount": "#t-queues",
        "items": [
          "Decouple / buffer / smooth: converts latency problem into throughput",
          "Message queue vs distributed log (replay, multiple consumer groups)",
          "Delivery: at-least-once is default; 'exactly-once' = at-least-once + idempotency",
          "Ordering only within a partition; partition by key; dead-letter queues",
          "Size consumers for average, let the queue absorb peaks, autoscale on depth",
          "Partitions >= max future consumers; monitor lag and oldest-message age"
        ]
      },
      {
        "group": "System-design framework",
        "slug": "system-design-framework",
        "mount": "#t-framework",
        "items": [
          "Requirements: functional vs non-functional; state what's out of scope",
          "Capacity estimation: QPS, storage, bandwidth, cache memory - tie each to a decision",
          "API design: endpoints, params, responses, errors before boxes",
          "High-level components: read path and write path data flow",
          "Deep dive: data model, partitioning, algorithm, consistency, failure modes",
          "Trade-offs: what you chose, what you gave up, what breaks at 10x"
        ]
      },
      {
        "group": "Worked example: URL shortener",
        "slug": "worked-example-url-shortener",
        "mount": "#t-url-shortener",
        "items": [
          "Requirements + the read:write = 100:1 assumption",
          "Capacity: 115k read QPS, 7-char base62 keyspace, ~75 GB hot cache",
          "API: POST /urls, GET /{code} 302, owner-only reads/delete",
          "Components: separate redirect service, read-through Redis, async analytics",
          "Key generation: hash vs counter+range vs key pool - pick counter+scramble",
          "Redirect path traced under the 50 ms p99 budget",
          "Failure modes: hot link, cache node loss, expiry cleanup, multi-region",
          "Trade-offs: 302 vs 301, cache is load-bearing, analytics best-effort"
        ]
      }
    ]
